From fb0c3ed6f83c0cb6274e200b7c089646a946dedb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:32:37 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] The direct link to a shown chat's computer is kept up, says
 which way it went, and skips host-only adapters

- A chat hosted on another of the person's computers, opened in a window,
  gets the direct link to that computer ready and keeps it up while it
  shows: zgx asks WarmDeviceLink when the chat opens and every 60 s after
  (the engine closes a link unused for five minutes), and stops when
  another chat opens there or the engine says there's no link to keep
  (hosted here, a host on the relay alone, an engine from before).
- Once a link is up, each end logs at INFO which way it went, from the
  ICE stats: "direct link up" with route = "host 192.168.1.20:50123 ->
  srflx 203.0.113.9:61002 udp, rtt 2 ms" (the selected candidate pair's
  types, addresses and ports, and its round trip). Peers::route gives the
  same line on demand. A slow link was otherwise a guess.
- On Windows, ICE no longer binds the host-only virtual switches WSL,
  Hyper-V, Docker Desktop, VirtualBox and VMware add (vEthernet (WSL),
  vEthernet (Default Switch), ...). Nothing else can reach them, and each
  connectivity check from them to another network failed with
  WSAENETUNREACH (10051), about fifty ERRORs a pairing. When no addresses
  were configured, PreviewService now passes the IPv4 addresses of the
  adapters that are up (GetAdaptersAddresses), minus those switches,
  instead of the 0.0.0.0 wildcard. A virtual switch with a default gateway
  stays (a Hyper-V external switch carries the real LAN on vEthernet), as
  does a tailnet's adapter. Read afresh for each connection. If the
  adapters can't be listed or nothing is left, the wildcard, as before.
  Elsewhere nothing changes. windows-sys gains the IpHelper, Ndis and
  Foundation features (no new crates).

Tests: peer's an_open_link_says_which_way_it_goes (a loopback pair: both
ends name the host pair); interfaces' host_only_switches_are_left_out_and_real_networks_kept
(the adapters of the desktop that logged the 10051s),
a_virtual_switch_carrying_the_lan_stays and
nothing_usable_binds_nothing_so_the_wildcard_stays. The Windows listing
type-checks for x86_64-pc-windows-msvc; it hasn't run on Windows yet.
